{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"04a973c9-9141-4e15-bc80-e778a0c07f62","hook_name":"SessionStart:startup","hook_event":"SessionStart","output":"# rabadon devridaim — rabadon-kosu2\nupdated: 2026-08-24T01:33:06Z\n\n## goal (as captured from the session)\nyani ne yapıcam\n\n## tests\nnot run this cycle\n\n## caught today (blocked before happening)\n- none\n\n## last moves\n- bash: claude help | grep -i update\n- bash: claude --help 2>&1 | head -50\n- bash: claude --help 2>&1 | grep -A2 -i \"update\\|autoupdate\"\n- Read: settings.json\n- bash: cd ~/damla_projects_2026/rabadon && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\nold=\"export PYTHO\n- Write: ONKONTROL.md\n- bash: export GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 GIT_PAGER=cat && git add reports/kosu/ONKONTROL.md \n- bash: brew install tmux 2>&1 | tail -4; echo ---; command -v tmux && tmux -V\n\n## for the next session\n- if tests are RED above: that is the open front — start there.\n- the guard is law (.rabadon/guard.json); rules born from incidents carry authoredBy: incident.\nrabadon: here is what I will do in this project.\n  check      : npm test --silent\n               (your own test suite; found via package.json scripts.test)\n  when       : NEVER — this project is in watch mode. I record what I would\n               have stopped and run nothing. `rabadon on` to enforce.\n  repair     : OFF. Turning it on spends money on YOUR account (it calls a model),\n               so I will not do it behind your back. Turn on: RABADON_JUDGE=1\n  scope      : ^native/, ^Makefile$, ^SPEC\\.md$, ^README\\.md$, ^docs/, ^hooks/, +4 more\n               (work outside this and I say something)\n  blind spots:\n               - an agent that calls a program by absolute path (/usr/bin/git) walks past me\n","stdout":"# rabadon devridaim — rabadon-kosu2\nupdated: 2026-08-24T01:33:06Z\n\n## goal (as captured from the session)\nyani ne yapıcam\n\n## tests\nnot run this cycle\n\n## caught today (blocked before happening)\n- none\n\n## last mo