{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xc6RFU9hCPz7CFv81A7YVr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# R7 acceptance — speed (a persistent daemon) and the two-armed proof.\n3\t#\n4\t# R7 has two halves and this file refuses to let either one carry the other.\n5\t#\n6\t#   SPEED. Most of the gate's wall clock is process startup: ~2.3 ms of a 4.2 ms\n7\t#   call is fork/exec/dyld (reports/R1.3/PROFIL.md). A persistent daemon\n8\t#   (rabadon-gated, unix socket) plus a thin client removes exactly that, so\n9\t#   judging costs the judging. If the daemon is absent the client falls back to\n10\t#   today's path — fail-SAME, not fail-open.\n11\t#\n12\t#   PROOF. One task set, two arms: A is the agent alone, B is the agent plus the\n13\t#   accumulation engine. The harness is REUSED (SWE-smith, or Terminal-Bench /\n14\t#   Harbor), never written here, and its full repo name and commit hash are\n15\t#   written under reports/R7/ or this script fails — see GOAL 4.\n16\t#\n17\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18\t# HOW THE < 1 ms CLAIM IS MEASURED, AND WHY NOT END-TO-END.\n19\t#\n20\t# Every budget claim in this file is measured by the instrument that makes the\n21\t# claim, and here that instrument is the IN-PROCESS probe of\n22\t# reports/R1.3/accept.sh (GOAL 4): a COPY of the shipped gate source is patched\n23\t# under /tmp with a steady_clock stamp at the top of main() and an atexit dump,\n24\t# and compiled there; native/ is never touched. End-to-end wall clock CANNOT\n25\t# settle this question, and not by a little: process spawn is ~2.3 ms of the\n26\t# 4.2 ms call, which is precisely the quantity the daemon deletes, so an\n27\t# end-to-end ruler would spend more than half its reading on the thing under\n28\t# test and its ±150 us noise floor would swamp a 1 ms ceiling. The R1.3\n29\t# planted-regression proof is the standard: that ruler caught a deliberate\n30\t# 150 us regression 7 of 7 while the end-to-end ruler missed it 3 of 8. No\n31\t# number below is asserted against a ceiling unless the probe produced it.\n32\t#\n33\t# The same reasoning is why GOAL 2c exists. R1.3 closed with a residual ~4%\n34\t# length dependence (3.5-4.9%, `last_ledger_mode()`'s whole-file fallback,\n35\t# +78.7 us, reports/R1.3/PROFIL.md) under a 10% ceiling. When the daemon removes\n36\t# process spawn the DENOMINATOR shrinks, so that percentage GROWS. KOSU-RABADON\n37\t# says R7 re-measures it in its own acceptance. That re-measurement is only\n38\t# meaningful with the daemon up, so it is bound to the daemon here.\n39\t#\n40\t# NO ASSERTION MAY PASS VACUOUSLY. A missing daemon, a missing harness name, a\n41\t# missing JSONL or an empty ledger is RED, never a skip. Where a file merely\n42\t# existing would be enough to go green, the check reads its CONTENT.\n43\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n44\tset -uo pipefail\n45\tHERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"; ROOT=\"$(cd \"$HERE/../..\" && pwd)\"; cd \"$ROOT\"\n46\tGATE=\"$ROOT/native/rabadon-gate\"\n47\tGATED=\"$ROOT/native/rabadon-gated\"\n48\tRD=\"$ROOT/reports/R7\"\n49\tP_N=0; F_N=0\n50\tpass(){ printf 'PASS  %s\\n' \"$1\"; P_N=$((P_N+1)); }\n51\tfail(){ printf 'FAIL  %s\\n' \"$1\"; F_N=$((F_N+1)); }\n52\tnote(){ printf '      %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\n53\thead_(){ printf '\\n== %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\n54\tW=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; trap 'rm -rf \"$W\"' EXIT\n55\tjstr(){ python3 -c 'import json,sys;print(json.dumps(sys.argv[1]))' \"$1\"; }\n56\t[ -x \"$GATE\" ] || { echo \"FAIL no gate binary — build first (make)\"; echo \"R7 NOT ACCEPTED\"; exit 1; }\n57\t\n58\tsb(){ H=\"$(mktemp -d \"$W/h.XXXXXX\")\"; PJ=\"$(mktemp -d \"$W/p.XXXXXX\")\"\n59\t  mkdir -p \"$H/.rabadon/spool\" \"$PJ/.git\"; printf 'ref: refs/heads/main\\n' >\"$PJ/.git/HEAD\"; : >\"$H/.rabadon/enabled\"; }\n60\tev(){ printf '{\"hook_event_name\":\"PreToolUse\",\"session_id\":\"%s\",\"cwd\":\"%s\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":%s}}' \\\n61\t  \"$1\" \"$PJ\" \"$(jstr \"$2\")\"; }\n62\t\n63\t############################################################################\n64\thead_ \"GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\"\n65\t# Three separate claims. A binary that exists but never binds a socket is not a\n66\t# daemon, and a client that runs the gate unconditionally is not a client.\n67\t\n68\tif [ -x \"$GATED\" ]; then\n69\t  pass \"1a rabadon-gated exists and is executable\"\n70\t  GATED_OK=1\n71\telse\n72\t  fail \"1a no rabadon-gated binary — the persistent daemon is not built\"\n73\t  note \"this is the whole speed half of R7; without it GOALs 2 and 3 measure nothing\"\n74\t  GATED_OK=0\n75\tfi\n76\t\n77\tGSRC=\"\"\n78\tfor c in native/gated.cpp native/daemon.cpp native/gated.h; do [ -f \"$c\" ] && GSRC=\"$c\" && break; done\n79\tif [ -n \"$GSRC\" ] && grep -q 'AF_UNIX' \"$GSRC\" && grep -qE '\\blisten\\s*\\(' \"$GSRC\"; then\n80\t  pass \"1b $GSRC binds and listens on a unix socket (a daemon, not a one-shot)\"\n81\telse\n82\t  fail \"1b no daemon source that binds AF_UNIX and listens\"\n83\t  note \"searched native/gated.cpp, native/daemon.cpp, native/gated.h\"\n84\tfi\n85\t\n86\t# The client must PREFER the socket and FALL BACK to today's in-process path.\n87\t# Fail-open (allow on daemon absence) is the one outcome that is worse than no\n88\t# daemon at all, so the check demands the fallback be visible in the source.\n89\tCSRC=\"\"\n90\tfor c in native/gate.cpp native/gated_client.h native/client.h; do\n91\t  [ -f \"$c\" ] && grep -q 'RABADON_GATED_SOCK\\|rabadon-gated.sock\\|gated.sock' \"$c\" && CSRC=\"$c\" && break\n92\tdone\n93\tif [ -n \"$CSRC\" ]; then\n94\t  pass \"1c a thin client path referencing the daemon socket exists ($CSRC)\"\n95\telse\n96\t  fail \"1c nothing in the gate reaches for a daemon socket — there is no thin client\"\n97\tfi\n98\t\n99\t############################################################################\n100\thead_ \"GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\"\n101\t# CEILING: 1000 us, from KOSU-RABADON R7 (\"daemon acikken kapi medyani < 1 ms\").\n102\t# Measured with the R1.3 in-process probe and nothing else — see the header.\n103\t# The probe is deliberately NOT built when the daemon is absent: building it\n104\t# would patch a copy of a gate source that has no daemon in it, and a median\n105\t# taken from that binary would be a number about today's gate wearing R7's\n106\t# label. A goal that cannot be measured is red, never skipped.\n107\tSOCK=\"$W/rabadon-gated.sock\"\n108\tDAEMON_UP=0\n109\tif [ \"$GATED_OK\" = 1 ]; then\n110\t  sb; DH=\"$H\"; DPJ=\"$PJ\"\n111\t  env HOME=\"$DH\" RABADON_DIR=\"$DH/.rabadon\" RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$GATED\" >\"$W/gated.log\" 2>&1 &\n112\t  DPID=$!\n113\t  for _ in $(seq 50); do [ -S \"$SOCK\" ] && DAEMON_UP=1 && break; done\n114\t  if [ \"$DAEMON_UP\" = 1 ]; then pass \"2a the daemon started and its socket is listening\"\n115\t  else fail \"2a rabadon-gated did not produce a listening socket at $SOCK\"; note \"$(tail -2 \"$W/gated.log\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; fi\n116\t  kill \"$DPID\" 2>/dev/null\n117\telse\n118\t  fail \"2a the daemon cannot be started — it does not exist\"\n119\tfi\n120\t\n121\tif [ \"$DAEMON_UP\" != 1 ]; then\n122\t  fail \"2b the < 1 ms median was NOT measured: no daemon to measure with\"\n123\t  note \"ceiling is 1000 us in-process; the instrument is the R1.3 probe (header)\"\n124\t  fail \"2c the residual length dependence was NOT re-measured under the daemon\"\n125\t  note \"R1.3 closed at 3.5-4.9% under a 10% ceiling with process spawn IN the\"\n126\t  note \"denominator; the daemon removes spawn, so the same absolute cost reads as\"\n127\t  note \"a LARGER percentage. The plan requires R7 to re-read it. Unread today.\"\n128\telse\n129\t  # Build the R1.3 probe against the daemon-aware gate source and take a median\n130\t  # over 300 warmed calls with the daemon up.\n131\t  PROBE_DIR=\"$W/probe\"; PGATE=\"$PROBE_DIR/rabadon-gate-probe\"; PROBE_OK=0\n132\t  mkdir -p \"$PROBE_DIR\" && cp native/*.h \"$PROBE_DIR\"/ 2>/dev/null\n133\t  python3 - native/gate.cpp \"$PROBE_DIR/gate_probe.cpp\" <<'PY' 2>/dev/null\n134\timport sys\n135\tsrc = open(sys.argv[1]).read()\n136\tPROBE = r'''\n137\t// ---- in-process probe, added to a COPY under /tmp by reports/R7/accept.sh ----\n138\t#include <chrono>\n139\tstatic std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point g_rbp_t0;\n140\tstatic void rbprobe_dump() {\n141\t  const char* p = getenv(\"RABADON_PROBE_OUT\");\n142\t  if (!p || !*p) return;\n143\t  const double us = std::chrono::duration<double, std::micro>(\n144\t      std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - g_rbp_t0).count();\n145\t  char buf[64];\n146\t  const int n = snprintf(buf, sizeof buf, \"%.1f\\n\", us);\n147\t  const int fd = open(p, O_WRONLY | O_APPEND | O_CREAT, 0644);\n148\t  if (fd < 0) return;\n149\t  ssize_t w = write(fd, buf, (size_t)n); (void)w;\n150\t  close(fd);\n151\t}\n152\tstatic void rbprobe_begin() { g_rbp_t0 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now(); atexit(rbprobe_dump); }\n153\t// ---- end probe ----\n154\t\n155\t'''\n156\ta = \"int main(int argc, char** argv) {\"\n157\tassert src.count(a) == 1, \"main() anchor is not unique\"\n158\topen(sys.argv[2], \"w\").write(src.replace(a, PROBE + a + \"\\n  rbprobe_begin();\"))\n159\tPY\n160\t  if [ -s \"$PROBE_DIR/gate_probe.cpp\" ] && \\\n161\t     ${CXX:-c++} -std=c++17 -O2 -I \"$PROBE_DIR\" -o \"$PGATE\" \"$PROBE_DIR/gate_probe.cpp\" 2>\"$W/probe.log\"; then PROBE_OK=1; fi\n162\t\n163\t  if [ \"$PROBE_OK\" != 1 ]; then\n164\t    fail \"2b the in-process instrument did not build — the median was NOT measured\"\n165\t    note \"$(tail -3 \"$W/probe.log\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n166\t    fail \"2c the residual length dependence was NOT re-measured (no instrument)\"\n167\t  else\n168\t    env HOME=\"$DH\" RABADON_DIR=\"$DH/.rabadon\" RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$GATED\" >>\"$W/gated.log\" 2>&1 &\n169\t    DPID=$!; for _ in $(seq 50); do [ -S \"$SOCK\" ] && break; done\n170\t    sb; EVX=\"$(ev speed 'echo hello world')\"; O=\"$W/med\"\n171\t    for _ in $(seq 60);  do printf '%s' \"$EVX\" | env HOME=\"$H\" RABADON_DIR=\"$H/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1; done\n172\t    for _ in $(seq 300); do printf '%s' \"$EVX\" | env HOME=\"$H\" RABADON_DIR=\"$H/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" RABADON_PROBE_OUT=\"$O\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1; done\n173\t    MED=\"$(python3 -c \"\n174\timport statistics,sys\n175\tv=[float(x) for x in open(sys.argv[1])] if __import__('os').path.exists(sys.argv[1]) else []\n176\tprint(f'{statistics.median(v):.1f}' if v else 'NONE')\" \"$O\")\"\n177\t    if [ \"$MED\" = NONE ]; then\n178\t      fail \"2b the probe produced no samples — the median was NOT measured\"\n179\t    else\n180\t      note \"in-process median with the daemon up: ${MED} us over 300 samples\"\n181\t      note \"ceiling = 1000 us (KOSU-RABADON R7); instrument = R1.3 in-process probe\"\n182\t      if [ \"$(python3 -c \"print(1 if float('$MED')<1000.0 else 0)\")\" = 1 ]; then\n183\t        pass \"2b the gate's median is ${MED} us with the daemon up, under the 1000 us ceiling\"\n184\t      else\n185\t        fail \"2b the gate's median is ${MED} us with the daemon up, ceiling is 1000 us\"\n186\t      fi\n187\t    fi\n188\t\n189\t    # 2c — re-measure the residual length dependence, daemon up. Same shape as\n190\t    # R1.3 GOAL 6: two sandboxes, one seeded to 50 events and one to 400, BOTH\n191\t    # seeded before EITHER is timed, then interleaved call by call so drift\n192\t    # lands on both arms in the same millisecond.\n193\t    sb; HA=\"$H\"; PA=\"$PJ\"; EVA=\"$(ev d 'echo hello world')\"\n194\t    sb; HB=\"$H\"; PB=\"$PJ\"; EVB=\"$(ev d 'echo hello world')\"\n195\t    for _ in $(seq 50);  do printf '%s' \"$EVA\" | env HOME=\"$HA\" RABADON_DIR=\"$HA/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1; done\n196\t    for _ in $(seq 400); do printf '%s' \"$EVB\" | env HOME=\"$HB\" RABADON_DIR=\"$HB/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1; done\n197\t    OA=\"$W/l50\"; OB=\"$W/l400\"\n198\t    for _ in $(seq 250); do\n199\t      printf '%s' \"$EVA\" | env HOME=\"$HA\" RABADON_DIR=\"$HA/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" RABADON_PROBE_OUT=\"$OA\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1\n200\t      printf '%s' \"$EVB\" | env HOME=\"$HB\" RABADON_DIR=\"$HB/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" RABADON_PROBE_OUT=\"$OB\" \"$PGATE\" >/dev/null 2>&1\n201\t    done\n202\t    R=\"$(python3 -c \"\n203\timport statistics,sys,os\n204\tdef r(p):\n205\t    return [float(x) for x in open(p)] if os.path.exists(p) else []\n206\ta,b=r(sys.argv[1]),r(sys.argv[2])\n207\tif not a or not b: print('NONE'); raise SystemExit\n208\tma,mb=statistics.median(a),statistics.median(b)\n209\tprint(f'{ma:.1f} {mb:.1f} {abs(mb-ma)/min(ma,mb)*100:.2f}')\" \"$OA\" \"$OB\")\"\n210\t    kill \"$DPID\" 2>/dev/null\n211\t    if [ \"$R\" = NONE ]; then\n212\t      fail \"2c the length-dependence re-measurement produced no samples\"\n213\t    else\n214\t      read -r M50 M400 PCT <<<\"$R\"\n215\t      note \"50-event session: ${M50} us   400-event session: ${M400} us   divergence ${PCT}%\"\n216\t      note \"R1.3 closed this at 3.5-4.9% WITH process spawn in the denominator\"\n217\t      # The number must be RECORDED, not just printed, because the plan asks R7\n218\t      # to carry it forward. A run that prints and forgets proves nothing later.\n219\t      if [ -f \"$RD/LENGTH.md\" ] && grep -qE '[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+%' \"$RD/LENGTH.md\"; then\n220\t        pass \"2c the residual length dependence is re-measured (${PCT}%) and written to reports/R7/LENGTH.md\"\n221\t      else\n222\t        fail \"2c measured ${PCT}% but reports/R7/LENGTH.md does not record it\"\n223\t      fi\n224\t    fi\n225\t  fi\n226\tfi\n227\t\n228\t############################################################################\n229\thead_ \"GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\"\n230\t# fail-SAME, not fail-open. Three surfaces, compared against the SAME gate run\n231\t# with no daemon variable set at all: exit code, ledger lines, refusal text.\n232\tif [ \"$GATED_OK\" != 1 ] || [ -z \"$CSRC\" ]; then\n233\t  fail \"3a exit codes with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED — there is no client path to compare\"\n234\t  fail \"3b ledger lines with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\"\n235\t  fail \"3c refusals with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\"\n236\t  note \"with no client, 'the daemon is down' is indistinguishable from today by\"\n237\t  note \"construction, and a comparison that cannot fail is not evidence\"\n238\telse\n239\t  DEAD=\"$W/definitely-not-a-socket.sock\"\n240\t  run3(){ # $1 = extra env; prints \"exit\\n<stdout>\\n---\\n<stderr>\"\n241\t    sb; local out err rc\n242\t    out=\"$(printf '%s' \"$(ev s7 \"$2\")\" | env HOME=\"$H\" RABADON_DIR=\"$H/.rabadon\" RABADON_NOTIFY=0 $1 \"$GATE\" 2>\"$W/e3\")\"; rc=$?\n243\t    printf '%s\\n%s\\n' \"$rc\" \"$out\"; cat \"$W/e3\"\n244\t    ls \"$H\"/.rabadon/spool/* >/dev/null 2>&1 && cat \"$H\"/.rabadon/spool/* | sed -E 's/\"ts\":[0-9]+/\"ts\":T/g; s/[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9:.]+Z?/TS/g'\n245\t  }\n246\t  for CMD in 'echo hello world' 'rm -rf /' 'git commit --no-verify -m x'; do\n247\t    A=\"$(run3 '' \"$CMD\")\"; B=\"$(run3 \"RABADON_GATED_SOCK=$DEAD\" \"$CMD\")\"\n248\t    if [ -z \"$A\" ]; then\n249\t      fail \"3-[$CMD] the baseline run produced nothing — an empty comparison is not a green\"\n250\t    elif [ \"$A\" = \"$B\" ]; then\n251\t      pass \"3-[$CMD] exit code, ledger lines and refusal text are byte-identical with the daemon down\"\n252\t    else\n253\t      fail \"3-[$CMD] behaviour diverges when the daemon is down — this is not fail-SAME\"\n254\t      diff <(printf '%s\\n' \"$A\") <(printf '%s\\n' \"$B\") | head -6 | sed 's/^/      /'\n255\t    fi\n256\t  done\n257\tfi\n258\t\n259\t############################################################################\n260\thead_ \"GOAL 4 — the harness is named, exactly, with its commit\"\n261\t# Terminal-Bench names four different things. Without the full repo name AND the\n262\t# commit, none of the five numbers is comparable to anything, so an unnamed\n263\t# harness fails the whole round rather than degrading it.\n264\tKNOWN='laude-institute/terminal-bench|harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2|harbor-framework/harbor|alibaba/terminal-bench-pro|SWE-bench/SWE-smith|swesmith/SWE-smith'\n265\tif [ -d \"$RD\" ]; then pass \"4a reports/R7/ exists\"; else fail \"4a reports/R7/ does not exist — nowhere for the evidence to land\"; fi\n266\tHFILE=\"\"\n267\tfor f in \"$RD\"/HARNESS.md \"$RD\"/harness.json \"$RD\"/HARNESS.txt; do [ -f \"$f\" ] && HFILE=\"$f\" && break; done\n268\tif [ -n \"$HFILE\" ] && grep -qE \"$KNOWN\" \"$HFILE\"; then\n269\t  pass \"4b the harness is named by full repo: $(grep -oE \"$KNOWN\" \"$HFILE\" | head -1)\"\n270\telse\n271\t  fail \"4b no reports/R7/HARNESS.md naming a known harness by org/repo\"\n272\t  note \"one of: laude-institute/terminal-bench, harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2,\"\n273\t  note \"harbor-framework/harbor, alibaba/terminal-bench-pro, SWE-smith\"\n274\tfi\n275\tif [ -n \"$HFILE\" ] && grep -qE '\\b[0-9a-f]{40}\\b' \"$HFILE\"; then\n276\t  pass \"4c the harness commit hash is pinned (40 hex)\"\n277\telse\n278\t  fail \"4c no 40-hex commit hash for the harness — 'Terminal-Bench' alone points at four repos\"\n279\tfi\n280\t# Cursor's 25.06 preparation, and its own honest label. Without it the agent\n281\t# finds the answer in the git history and BOTH arms inflate, which does not show\n282\t# up as a bug — it shows up as two good-looking numbers.\n283\tif [ -n \"$HFILE\" ] && grep -qi 'git' \"$HFILE\" && grep -qiE 'egress|network' \"$HFILE\" && grep -qi 'best.effort' \"$HFILE\"; then\n284\t  pass \"4d the Cursor preparation is recorded: .git cleaned, egress closed, labelled best-effort\"\n285\telse\n286\t  fail \"4d the .git-cleaning / egress-closing preparation is not recorded (with its best-effort label)\"\n287\tfi\n288\t\n289\t############################################################################\n290\thead_ \"GOAL 5 — the raw run lands here, and can be re-run\"\n291\tJL=\"$(ls \"$RD\"/*.jsonl 2>/dev/null | head -1)\"\n292\tif [ -n \"$JL\" ] && [ -s \"$JL\" ]; then\n293\t  pass \"5a raw JSONL is under reports/R7/ and is not empty ($(basename \"$JL\"))\"\n294\telse\n295\t  fail \"5a no non-empty *.jsonl under reports/R7/ — a summary is not the evidence\"\n296\tfi\n297\tif [ -n \"$JL\" ] && [ -s \"$JL\" ]; then\n298\t  S=\"$(python3 - \"$JL\" <<'PY'\n299\timport json,sys,collections\n300\tarms=collections.defaultdict(set)\n301\tn=0\n302\tfor line in open(sys.argv[1]):\n303\t    line=line.strip()\n304\t    if not line: continue\n305\t    try: r=json.loads(line)\n306\t    except Exception: continue\n307\t    n+=1\n308\t    a=str(r.get(\"arm\",\"\")).upper()\n309\t    t=r.get(\"task\") or r.get(\"task_id\") or r.get(\"instance_id\")\n310\t    if a and t: arms[a].add(str(t))\n311\tok = set(arms)>={\"A\",\"B\"} and min((len(v) for v in arms.values()), default=0)>=2\n312\tprint(\"OK\" if ok else \"BAD\", n, len(arms.get(\"A\",())), len(arms.get(\"B\",())))\n313\tPY\n314\t)\"\n315\t  read -r VERD NREC NA NB <<<\"$S\"\n316\t  note \"records: $NREC   distinct tasks — arm A: $NA, arm B: $NB\"\n317\t  if [ \"$VERD\" = OK ]; then\n318\t    pass \"5b both arms are present per-task in the raw records (A:$NA tasks, B:$NB tasks)\"\n319\t  else\n320\t    fail \"5b the JSONL is not a two-armed per-task record (A:$NA tasks, B:$NB tasks)\"\n321\t  fi\n322\telse\n323\t  fail \"5b no JSONL to check for two arms\"\n324\tfi\n325\t# bench/reproduce.sh already exists for other numbers, so its mere existence is\n326\t# a vacuous green here. It must actually re-run THIS run.\n327\tif [ -f bench/reproduce.sh ] && grep -qiE 'R7|two.arm|arm B' bench/reproduce.sh; then\n328\t  pass \"5c bench/reproduce.sh re-runs the two-armed run\"\n329\telse\n330\t  fail \"5c bench/reproduce.sh exists but says nothing about R7's two-armed run\"\n331\tfi\n332\t\n333\t############################################################################\n334\thead_ \"GOAL 6 — the five numbers, each of them, from the raw data\"\n335\tFIVE=\"$W/five\"\n336\tif [ -n \"$JL\" ] && [ -s \"$JL\" ]; then\n337\t  python3 - \"$JL\" >\"$FIVE\" 2>/dev/null <<'PY'\n338\timport json,sys,collections\n339\trows=[]\n340\tfor line in open(sys.argv[1]):\n341\t    line=line.strip()\n342\t    if not line: continue\n343\t    try: rows.append(json.loads(line))\n344\t    except Exception: pass\n345\tdef arm(a): return [r for r in rows if str(r.get(\"arm\",\"\")).upper()==a]\n346\tout={}\n347\tfor a in (\"A\",\"B\"):\n348\t    R=arm(a)\n349\t    if not R: continue\n350\t    fixed=[r for r in R if \"heldout_pass\" in r]\n351\t    out[f\"fix_{a}\"]=(sum(1 for r in fixed if r[\"heldout_pass\"])/len(fixed)*100) if fixed else None\n352\t    out[f\"heldout_{a}\"]=len(fixed)\n353\t    tk=[r.get(\"tokens\") for r in R if isinstance(r.get(\"tokens\"),(int,float))]\n354\t    out[f\"tok_{a}\"]=sum(tk) if tk else None\n355\t    iv=[r.get(\"interventions\") for r in R if isinstance(r.get(\"interventions\"),(int,float))]\n356\t    out[f\"iv_{a}\"]=sum(iv) if iv else None\n357\t    fp=[r.get(\"false_positive\") for r in R if r.get(\"false_positive\") is not None]\n358\t    out[f\"fp_{a}\"]=(sum(1 for x in fp if x)/len(fp)*100) if fp else None\n359\test=[r.get(\"estimated_saved\") for r in arm(\"B\") if isinstance(r.get(\"estimated_saved\"),(int,float))]\n360\tout[\"est\"]=sum(est) if est else None\n361\tfor k,v in out.items():\n362\t    print(k, \"NONE\" if v is None else f\"{v:.4f}\")\n363\tPY\n364\tfi\n365\tg(){ awk -v k=\"$1\" '$1==k{print $2}' \"$FIVE\" 2>/dev/null; }\n366\thave(){ v=\"$(g \"$1\")\"; [ -n \"$v\" ] && [ \"$v\" != NONE ]; }\n367\t\n368\tif have fix_A && have fix_B && [ \"$(g heldout_A)\" != 0 ] && [ \"$(g heldout_B)\" != 0 ]; then\n369\t  pass \"6a real fix rate from a HELD-OUT test: A $(g fix_A)% / B $(g fix_B)% ($(g heldout_A)+$(g heldout_B) judged)\"\n370\telse\n371\t  fail \"6a no held-out fix rate in the raw data (field 'heldout_pass' per task, both arms)\"\n372\t  note \"the agent's own test does not count — that is the metric it is optimising\"\n373\tfi\n374\tif have tok_A && have tok_B; then pass \"6b tokens spent: A $(g tok_A) / B $(g tok_B)\"\n375\telse fail \"6b token totals are missing from the raw data\"; fi\n376\tif have iv_A && have iv_B; then pass \"6c human interventions: A $(g iv_A) / B $(g iv_B)\"\n377\telse fail \"6c human intervention counts are missing from the raw data\"; fi\n378\tif have fp_A && have fp_B; then pass \"6d false positive rate: A $(g fp_A)% / B $(g fp_B)%\"\n379\telse fail \"6d false positive rates are missing from the raw data\"; fi\n380\tif have est && have tok_A && have tok_B; then\n381\t  DEV=\"$(python3 -c \"\n382\te=float('$(g est)'); real=float('$(g tok_A)')-float('$(g tok_B)')\n383\tprint('NODIFF' if real==0 else f'{abs(e-real)/abs(real)*100:.1f}')\")\"\n384\t  if [ \"$DEV\" = NODIFF ]; then\n385\t    fail \"6e the two arms spent identical tokens — the counter cannot be validated against a zero difference\"\n386\t  else\n387\t    pass \"6e counter validation: estimate $(g est) vs real difference $(python3 -c \"print(float('$(g tok_A)')-float('$(g tok_B)'))\"), deviation ${DEV}%\"\n388\t  fi\n389\telse\n390\t  fail \"6e counter validation impossible: no 'estimated_saved' total on arm B, or no token totals\"\n391\t  DEV=\"\"\n392\tfi\n393\t\n394\t############################################################################\n395\thead_ \"GOAL 7 — the falsification conditions are checkable, and checked\"\n396\t# These are the plan's own conditions, written before the result was seen. They\n397\t# are part of THIS round: a run that cannot evaluate them has not tested the\n398\t# thesis, it has only produced numbers.\n399\tif have fix_A && have fix_B && have tok_A && have tok_B; then\n400\t  V=\"$(python3 -c \"\n401\tfa,fb=float('$(g fix_A)'),float('$(g fix_B)'); ta,tb=float('$(g tok_A)'),float('$(g tok_B)')\n402\tprint('IMPROVED' if (fb>fa or tb<ta) else 'FLAT')\")\"\n403\t  if [ \"$V\" = IMPROVED ]; then\n404\t    pass \"7a falsification 1 evaluated: arm B improves on fix rate or net tokens — the injection thesis stands\"\n405\t  else\n406\t    fail \"7a falsification 1 TRIGGERED: arm B improves neither real fix rate nor net tokens\"\n407\t    note \"per KOSU-RABADON, the injection thesis is wrong; the accumulation engine\"\n408\t    note \"goes silent and the product position is rethought. The M3 piece still ships.\"\n409\t  fi\n410\telse\n411\t  fail \"7a falsification 1 is UNCHECKABLE — the numbers it needs are not in the data\"\n412\tfi\n413\tif [ -n \"${DEV:-}\" ] && [ \"$DEV\" != NODIFF ]; then\n414\t  if [ \"$(python3 -c \"print(1 if float('$DEV')<=50.0 else 0)\")\" = 1 ]; then\n415\t    pass \"7b falsification 2 evaluated: counter deviates ${DEV}%, at or under 50% — the dollar line may be published\"\n416\t  else\n417\t    fail \"7b falsification 2 TRIGGERED: counter deviates ${DEV}% from the real token difference (limit 50%)\"\n418\t    note \"the dollar line comes out of the closing line, the README and the landing\"\n419\t    note \"page the same day; only the error count stays until the formula is refixed\"\n420\t  fi\n421\telse\n422\t  fail \"7b falsification 2 is UNCHECKABLE — no deviation could be computed\"\n423\tfi\n424\t\n425\t############################################################################\n426\thead_ \"GOAL 8 — nothing already standing fell over\"\n427\tif OUT=\"$(./native/moves_test.sh 2>&1)\" && printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | grep -q 'moves: 21 passed, 0 failed'; then\n428\t  pass \"8a native/moves_test.sh 21/0\"\n429\telse\n430\t  fail \"8a native/moves_test.sh is not 21 passed / 0 failed: $(printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | tail -1)\"\n431\tfi\n432\tif OUT=\"$(./native/signals_test.sh 2>&1)\" && printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | grep -q 'signals: 39 passed, 0 failed'; then\n433\t  pass \"8b native/signals_test.sh 39/0\"\n434\telse\n435\t  fail \"8b native/signals_test.sh is not 39 passed / 0 failed: $(printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | tail -1)\"\n436\tfi\n437\tif OUT=\"$(./reports/R2/accept.sh 2>&1)\" && printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | grep -q 'R2 acceptance: 19 green, 0 red'; then\n438\t  pass \"8c reports/R2/accept.sh 19 green, 0 red\"\n439\telse\n440\t  fail \"8c reports/R2/accept.sh is not 19 green / 0 red: $(printf '%s' \"$OUT\" | grep 'acceptance:' | tail -1)\"\n441\tfi\n442\t\n443\tprintf '\\n== R7 acceptance: %d green, %d red\\n' \"$P_N\" \"$F_N\"\n444\t[ \"$F_N\" -gt 0 ] && { printf 'R7 NOT ACCEPTED\\n'; exit 1; }\n445\tprintf 'R7 ACCEPTED\\n'; exit 0\n446\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015nSj3ZfDHCPqUgndMzERuW","session_id":"e644857f-2533-466c-b42f-f6dc07805f84","uuid":"5db4ff6e-9a87-42b5-984b-38cb49515b9b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:46:46.896Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Survey R7 acceptance state"}
