{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G38q2UPerrHQHxCTEXfi7x","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/chain.h:// out to a socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/temp_root_glob_test.sh:# and a database socket are gone. A rule that refuses the root and waives its\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/temp_root_glob_test.sh:mkdir -p \"$SHARED/other-session\" \"$SHARED/db-sockets\"\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/temp_root_glob_test.sh:FOREIGN=$(grep -c -e 'other-session' -e 'db-sockets' \"$LAB/argv.log\")\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/temp_root_glob_test.sh:ANCHORED_FOREIGN=$(grep -c -e 'other-session' -e 'db-sockets' \"$LAB/argv.log\")\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/sigpipe_test.sh:# regression (adversarial-hunt CRITICAL): a DEAD watcher socket must never turn\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/sigpipe_test.sh:# a block into an allow. The gate emits its verdict over the unix socket BEFORE\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/sigpipe_test.sh:# exit(2); a peer-closed socket used to raise SIGPIPE and kill the gate\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/sigpipe_test.sh:import socket, os, sys, time\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/sigpipe_test.sh:s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/script_wrapper_test.sh:# without one it dies with \"tcgetattr/ioctl: Operation not supported on socket\"\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/pathres.h://     database socket. Refusing the root and waiving its contents was the hole\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/bench.py:    # spool/socket at a throwaway dir so the real ledger stays clean by\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/cli_help.h:// Call this as the FIRST statement of main, before any file, socket, model or\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:// rabadon-serve — the team ledger. C++17, POSIX sockets, zero dependencies.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:#include <sys/socket.h>\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:  // thread-per-connection pool, so every second spent blocked on an idle socket\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:  \"  -h, --help    this screen. no socket is opened.\\n\"\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:  // parser, and started listening. A help request must never open a socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:    // stranger's terminal froze on a listening socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:  int lfd = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve.cpp:  if (lfd < 0) { perror(\"socket\"); return 1; }\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/serve_test.sh:# running the real server over a real socket. No mocks: a live process, real\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:// the unix socket. The deterministic PreToolUse path lives here entirely; the\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:#include <sys/socket.h>\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:// ---------- spool + socket emit ----------\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:    sockFd = socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:    struct sockaddr_un addr; memset(&addr, 0, sizeof(addr));\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:    addr.sun_family = AF_UNIX;\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:  // SECURITY, fail-CLOSED: the gate emits its verdict over a unix socket to any\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:  // rabadon home (spool/socket) — env override mirrors core/bus.mjs\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs:// happens, over a unix domain socket, to any attached `rabadon watch`.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs://      to a local spool file, and the number of socket drops is COUNTED and\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs:// Topology: `rabadon watch` OWNS the socket (server). Pipelines are clients:\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs: * (newline included) so the caller can fan the same bytes to the socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs:    sock.unref(); // the socket must never keep the pipeline process alive\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs:    // spool first — the spool is the source of truth, the socket is the live\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs: * Start the watch server (used by `rabadon watch`). Owns the socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs:  // a stale socket file from a killed watcher would block bind — remove it,\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.test.mjs:// rabadon bus tests — the live stream proven over a real unix socket.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.test.mjs:test('events flow pipeline -> socket -> watcher, in order, parsed', async () => {\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/bin/rabadon.mjs:// happens — pushed over a unix socket, not polled from a file.\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/bin/rabadon.mjs:    `  ${paint(C.dim, `socket: ${SOCK_PATH}`)}`,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015nSj3ZfDHCPqUgndMzERuW","session_id":"e644857f-2533-466c-b42f-f6dc07805f84","uuid":"ca33ab9e-3c84-4148-b167-099114473832","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:46:48.399Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Survey R7 acceptance state"}
