{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nSj3ZfDHCPqUgndMzERuW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the final report.\n\n---\n\n## R7 Round Status Report\n\n**1. Does reports/R7/accept.sh exist? What checks does it verify?**\n\nYes. The script checks 8 GOALs:\n- GOAL 1: daemon binary (rabadon-gated) exists + has AF_UNIX socket code + client path referencing socket exists\n- GOAL 2a-c: daemon starts, socket listens, median < 1 ms (in-process probe), residual length dependence re-measured with daemon up\n- GOAL 3a-c: daemon down → byte-identical behavior (exit codes, ledger lines, refusal text) vs baseline\n- GOAL 4a-d: harness named (known repo) + commit hash pinned (40 hex) + Cursor preparation recorded (git cleaned, egress closed, best-effort label)\n- GOAL 5a-c: raw non-empty JSONL under reports/R7/, both arms present (A+B, ≥2 tasks each), bench/reproduce.sh re-runs two-armed run\n- GOAL 6a-e: held-out fix rate, token totals, intervention counts, false positive rates, counter validation (estimated vs real difference ≤50% dev)\n- GOAL 7a-b: falsification conditions checkable (arm B improves fix rate OR reduces tokens; counter deviation ≤50%)\n- GOAL 8a-c: regression check (moves_test 21/0, signals_test 39/0, R2 accept 19/0)\n\n**2. Files under reports/R7/**\n\n/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/reports/R7/accept.sh (23,564 bytes, executable)\n\nOnly accept.sh exists; no other files present (no DENEMELER.md, no HARNESS.md, no raw JSONL, no LENGTH.md).\n\n**3. Daemon/socket code in native/, core/, bin/**\n\nFound references but NOT complete daemon implementation:\n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp`: AF_UNIX socket setup (sockaddr_un, socket(), connect path with RABADON_GATED_SOCK fallback)\n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/core/bus.mjs`: Unix socket server/client (watch server owns socket)\n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/bin/rabadon.mjs`: Socket path output (SOCK_PATH reference)\n\nNo rabadon-gated binary or daemon.cpp found in native/.\n\n**4. DENEMELER.md under reports/R7**\n\nNo. Only accept.sh exists.\n\n**5. R7 acceptance requirements (KOSU-RABADON.md §R7)**\n\n- Daemon running → gate median < 1 ms (in-process probe, not end-to-end)\n- Daemon down → byte-identical behavior vs today (fail-SAME, not fail-open)\n- Two-armed raw JSONL + reproduce.sh re-runnable\n- Harness fully named (org/repo + 40-hex commit hash) + Cursor prep recorded (git cleaned, egress closed, best-effort label)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e644857f-2533-466c-b42f-f6dc07805f84","uuid":"b5da7363-e6d9-4418-847f-c473d7d99a08","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:47:10.070Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo /Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2, inspect the R7 round's current state. Do NOT modify anything. Report back at most 15 lines total:\n\n1. Does reports/R7/accept.sh exist? What exactly does it check (list its checks as short bullets)?\n2. What files exist under reports/R7/ ?\n3. Is there any daemon / unix-socket code in the repo already (search native/, core/, bin/ for socket/AF_UNIX/sockaddr_un/daemon)? Give file:line for anything found.\n4. Does reports/R7/ contain a DENEMELER.md?\n5. Search KOSU-RABADON.md for the \"R7\" section and summarize its acceptance requirements in 3-4 bullets.\n\nBe terse. File paths + facts only, no advice.","agentId":"a26682d4a8a0caa1f","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the final report.\n\n---\n\n## R7 Round Status Report\n\n**1. Does reports/R7/accept.sh exist? What checks does it verify?**\n\nYes. The script checks 8 GOALs:\n- GOAL 1: daemon binary (rabadon-gated) exists + has AF_UNIX socket code + client path referencing socket exists\n- GOAL 2a-c: daemon starts, soc